   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Indirect questions",
   "texto": [
    "To say «Yes» within a sentence, **-는지** is used with verbs in present (**오는지** = if it comes), **-았/었는지** in past (**왔는지** = if it came) and **-(으)ㄹ지** for something future or uncertain (**올지** = if it will come). With adjectives: **-(으)ㄴ지** present (**좋은지**) and **-았/었는지** past (**좋았는지**); with names, **-(이)ㄴ지** (**학생인지**).",
    "이 답이 **맞는지** 모르겠어요 = no sé si esta respuesta es correcta."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Present alternatives",
   "texto": [
    "To ask if one option or another is met, the forms can be repeated: The full sentence usually carries a verb like **알다, 모르다, 묻다** or **궁금하다**.",
    "With speaking verbs, **-는지** expresses the indirect question; it is not the marker to quote literally an affirmation."
